{"id": "EUVD-2026-99250", "enisaUuid": "12c5af4e-3f94-31f1-9a0a-559108d3f872", "description": "Stonewuu ai-fusion-video through 1.2.0 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows authenticated non-admin users to read stored secrets through unprotected ApiConfigController and SystemConfigController endpoints. Attackers can query the api-config get/list and system config endpoints to obtain AI provider API keys, proxy passwords and mail_password, enabling billing abuse and sending mail as the platform.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:32:38", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/ai-fusion-video-broken-access-control-and-upload-path-traversal", "https://github.com/Stonewuu/ai-fusion-video/blob/v1.2.0/ai-fusion-video/src/main/java/com/stonewu/fusion/controller/ai/ApiConfigController.java#L81-L102", "https://github.com/Stonewuu/ai-fusion-video/blob/v1.2.0/ai-fusion-video/src/main/java/com/stonewu/fusion/controller/system/SystemConfigController.java#L26-L36", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ai-fusion-video-through-1.2.0-missing-authorization-in-configuration-read-endpoints-exposes-stored-credentials"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110209", "GHSA-4mgp-pq8c-xqfr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8a9e2706-90ff-3855-bea1-f0e65a785fbb", "product": {"name": "ai-fusion-video", "vendor": {"name": "Stonewuu"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "84e57729-e131-3935-afc2-41bcbead4ba4", "vendor": {"name": "Stonewuu"}}], "isExploited": false}